<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27999" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόναξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκος</span>, ὁ, poet. gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δούνακος</span>
		<u>AP</u> (v. infr.), dat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώνακι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δονέω,</span> 'a reed
				<i>shaken with the wind'):—pole-reed, Arundo
			Donax,</i> smaller than the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλαμος</span> (Eust.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1165.23
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.467
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.474
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.11.11
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόνακες καλάμοιο</span>
				reed-<i>stalks,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				47
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bed of reeds,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				3.67
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>anything made of reed,</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>shaft of an arrow,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.584
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shepherd's pipe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.25
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				574
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				20.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>fishing-rod</i> or <i>limed reed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.702
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>bridge</i> of the lyre, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				232
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> shell-fish, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σωλήν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.Siph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.90d
			</span></i>.</div>
